J. Meditation states and traits: EEG, ERP, and neuroimaging studies. <em>Psychol Bull</em>. 2006 3; 132(2): 180–211.</div><div class="external-links"><div class="core-xlink-crossref"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1037/0033-2909.132.2.180">Crossref</a></div><div class="core-xlink-pubmed"><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16536641/">PubMed</a></div><div class="core-xlink-isi"><a href="https://gateway.webofknowledge.com/gateway/Gateway.cgi?GWVersion=2&amp;DestApp=WOS_CPL&amp;UsrCustomerID=5e3815c904498985e796fc91436abd9a&amp;SrcAuth=atyponcel&amp;SrcApp=literatum&amp;DestLinkType=FullRecord&amp;KeyUT=WOS%3A000236226500002">Web of Science</a></div><div class="core-xlink-google-scholar"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=Meditation+states+and+traits%3A+EEG%2C+ERP%2C+and+neuroimaging+studies&amp;author=BR+Cahn&amp;author=J+Polich&amp;publication_year=2006&amp;journal=Psychol+Bull&amp;pages=180-211&amp;doi=10.1037%2F0033-2909.132.2.180&amp;pmid=16536641">Google Scholar</a></div></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem"><div id="bibr8-2156587216668109" class="citations"><div class="citation"><div class="citation-content"><span class="label">8.</span> Melville GW, Chang D, Colagiuri B, Marshall PW, Cheema BS. Fifteen minutes of chair-based yoga postures or guided meditation performed in the office can elicit a relaxation response. <em>Evid Based Complement Alternat Med</em>. 2012; Article ID 501986. doi:10.1155/2012/501986</div><div class="external-links"><div class="core-xlink-crossref"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1155/2012/501986">Crossref</a></div><div class="core-xlink-pubmed"><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22291847/">PubMed</a></div><div class="core-xlink-isi"><a href="https://gateway.webofknowledge.com/gateway/Gateway.cgi?GWVersion=2&amp;DestApp=WOS_CPL&amp;UsrCustomerID=5e3815c904498985e796fc91436abd9a&amp;SrcAuth=atyponcel&amp;SrcApp=literatum&amp;DestLinkType=FullRecord&amp;KeyUT=000299532600001">Web of Science</a></div><div class="core-xlink-google-scholar"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=Fifteen+minutes+of+chair-based+yoga+postures+or+guided+meditation+performed+in+the+office+can+elicit+a+relaxation+response&amp;author=GW+Melville&amp;author=D+Chang&amp;author=B+Colagiuri&amp;author=PW+Marshall&amp;author=BS+Cheema&amp;publication_year=2012&amp;journal=Evid+Based+Complement+Alternat+Med&amp;doi=10.1155%2F2012%2F501986&amp;pmid=22291847">Google Scholar</a></div></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem"><div id="bibr9-2156587216668109" class="citations"><div class="citation"><div class="citation-content"><span class="label">9.</span> Benson H. <em>The Relaxation Response</em>. New York: Morrow: 1975.</div><div class="external-links"><div class="core-xlink-google-scholar"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=The+Relaxation+Response&amp;author=H+Benson&amp;publication_year=1975">Google Scholar</a></div></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem"><div id="bibr10-2156587216668109" class="citations"><div class="citation"><div class="citation-content"><span class="label">10.</span> Dusek JA, Otu HH, Wohlhueter AL, et al. Genomic counter-stress changes induced by the relaxation response. <em>PloS one</em>. 2008 7 2;3(7): e2576.</div><div class="external-links"><div class="core-xlink-crossref"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0002576">Crossref</a></div><div class="core-xlink-pubmed"><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18596974/">PubMed</a></div><div class="core-xlink-isi"><a href="https://gateway.webofknowledge.com/gateway/Gateway.cgi?GWVersion=2&amp;DestApp=WOS_CPL&amp;UsrCustomerID=5e3815c904498985e796fc91436abd9a&amp;SrcAuth=atyponcel&amp;SrcApp=literatum&amp;DestLinkType=FullRecord&amp;KeyUT=000263288200041">Web of Science</a></div><div class="core-xlink-google-scholar"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=Genomic+counter-stress+changes+induced+by+the+relaxation+response&amp;author=JA+Dusek&amp;author=HH+Otu&amp;author=AL+Wohlhueter&amp;publication_year=2008&amp;journal=PloS+one&amp;pages=e2576&amp;doi=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0002576&amp;pmid=18596974">Google Scholar</a></div></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem"><div id="bibr11-2156587216668109" class="citations"><div class="citation"><div class="citation-content"><span class="label">11.</span> Park ER, Traeger L, Vranceanu AM, Scult M, Lerner JA, Benson H, Denninger J, Fricchione GL. The development of a patient-centered program based on the relaxation response: The Relaxation Response Resiliency Program (3RP). <em>Psychosomatics</em>. 2013; 54:165–174.</div><div class="external-links"><div class="core-xlink-crossref"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.psym.2012.09.001">Crossref</a></div><div class="core-xlink-pubmed"><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23352048/">PubMed</a></div><div class="core-xlink-isi"><a href="https://gateway.webofknowledge.com/gateway/Gateway.cgi?GWVersion=2&amp;DestApp=WOS_CPL&amp;UsrCustomerID=5e3815c904498985e796fc91436abd9a&amp;SrcAuth=atyponcel&amp;SrcApp=literatum&amp;DestLinkType=FullRecord&amp;KeyUT=000315975300009">Web of Science</a></div><div class="core-xlink-google-scholar"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=The+development+of+a+patient-centered+program+based+on+the+relaxation+response%3A+The+Relaxation+Response+Resiliency+Program+%283RP%29&amp;author=ER+Park&amp;author=L+Traeger&amp;author=AM+Vranceanu&amp;author=M+Scult&amp;author=JA+Lerner&amp;author=H+Benson&amp;author=J+Denninger&amp;author=GL+Fricchione&amp;publication_year=2013&amp;journal=Psychosomatics&amp;pages=165-174&amp;doi=10.1016%2Fj.psym.2012.09.001&amp;pmid=23352048">Google Scholar</a></div></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem"><div id="bibr12-2156587216668109" class="citations"><div class="citation"><div class="citation-content"><span class="label">12.</span> Gaynor ML. Sounds of healing: A physician reveals the therapeutic power of sound, voice, and music. New York: Broadway Books; 1999.</div><div class="external-links"><div class="core-xlink-google-scholar"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=Sounds+of+healing%3A+A+physician+reveals+the+therapeutic+power+of+sound%2C+voice%2C+and+music&amp;author=ML+Gaynor&amp;publication_year=1999">Google Scholar</a></div></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem"><div id="bibr13-2156587216668109" class="citations"><div class="citation"><div class="citation-content"><span class="label">13.</span> Perry F. Himalyan sound revelations: The complete singing bowl book. London: Polair Publishing, 2014.</div><div class="external-links"><div class="core-xlink-google-scholar"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=Himalyan+sound+revelations%3A+The+complete+singing+bowl+book&amp;author=F+Perry&amp;publication_year=2014">Google Scholar</a></div></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem"><div id="bibr14-2156587216668109" class="citations"><div class="citation"><div class="citation-content"><span class="label">14.</span> Burtner M, Serafin S, Topper D. Real-time spatial processing and transformations of a singing bowl. In Proceedings of the 5th International Conference on Digital Audio Effects (DAFx-02) 2002 Sep 26 (pp. 123–126).</div><div class="external-links"><div class="core-xlink-google-scholar"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=Real-time+spatial+processing+and+transformations+of+a+singing+bowl&amp;author=M+Burtner&amp;author=S+Serafin&amp;author=D+Topper&amp;pages=123-126">Google Scholar</a></div></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem"><div id="bibr15-2156587216668109" class="citations"><div class="citation"><div class="citation-content"><span class="label">15.</span> Inácio O, Henrique LL, Antunes J. The dynamics of Tibetan singing bowls. <em>Acta Acustica United with Acustica</em>. 2006 7 1;92(4):637–53.</div><div class="external-links"><div class="core-xlink-isi"><a href="https://gateway.webofknowledge.com/gateway/Gateway.cgi?GWVers